    ["我和几个学员从昨晚开始就在收拾东西，很快就能离开这诡异的地方了。\n昨晚，有两位研究员先生消失了，还有几个人因为害怕而跑出了营地，我认为这并不是理智的选择，因为野外的环境更加恶劣。\n我能看得出来曼斯教授也十分不安，但他是我们一行人的主心骨。他今天看起来是强撑着下达的指示，毕竟对于人类而言——未知是最古老最强烈的恐惧，就连曼斯教授也不例外。\n稍后，我们将消耗一部分带来的食物（这将减少我们行李的重量），然后我们就会启程。\n\n我决定一路记录下目前所见的一切，因为就在刚才，我看见一个活生生的人，从我眼前消失。我已经做好最坏的打算，或许这本日记将是我留在这个世界上的最后一抹痕迹。\n\n一旁的学员转过头对我说，曼斯教授也不见了，下一个会（日记戛然而止）"] = "A few students and I have been packing since last night, and we will soon be able to leave this eerie place. \n Last night, two researchers disappeared, and several others ran out of the camp out of fear. I don't think this is a rational choice, as the environment in the wild is even harsher. \n I can tell that Professor Mans is also very uneasy, but he is the backbone of our group. He seems to be forcing himself to give instructions today; after all, for humans—the unknown is the oldest and most intense fear, and Professor Mans is no exception. \n Later, we will consume some of the food we brought (which will reduce the weight of our luggage), and then we will set off. \n \n I have decided to record everything I see along the way, because just a moment ago, I saw a living person disappear right before my eyes. I have prepared for the worst; perhaps this diary will be the last trace I leave in this world. \n \n The student beside me turned to me and said that Professor Mans is also gone, and the next one will be (diary ends abruptly)",
